q 0 0 0 RG 54.00 680.35 504.00 15.22 re S Q
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 684.35 Tm (State examiners in Utah, Tennessee, South Carolina and Texas agree with advisors at SimekScott, Friedman,) Tj ET
q 0 0 0 RG 54.00 665.12 504.00 15.22 re S Q
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 669.12 Tm (Kodiak and Clarus on what triggers audits: non-filing, missing industry property types, and M&A. They also agree) Tj ET
q 0 0 0 RG 54.00 649.90 504.00 15.22 re S Q
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 653.90 Tm (that receivable credit balances are where the real exposure hides. The mechanics run on hard numbers. Tennessee) Tj ET
q 0 0 0 RG 54.00 634.67 504.00 15.22 re S Q
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 638.67 Tm (penalizes willful failure at $1,000 a day up to $25,000 plus 25 percent of the property value. South Carolina) Tj ET
q 0 0 0 RG 54.00 619.45 504.00 15.22 re S Q
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 623.45 Tm (requires letters on items of $50 or more, sent no more than 120 days before filing. Texas sets a $250 notice floor) Tj ET
q 0 0 0 RG 54.00 604.22 504.00 15.22 re S Q
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 608.22 Tm (and a July 1 deadline. Delaware gives VDA invitees 90 days before referring them to audit. Voluntary disclosure) Tj ET
q 0 0 0 RG 54.00 589.00 504.00 15.22 re S Q
