BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (Once an audit lands, the record-retention gap becomes the loss engine. Friedman LLP reports contingency-fee auditors) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (looking for records that go back 20 years, a five-year dormancy period plus fifteen years of look-back, and when) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (records are gone the holder falls into an estimation fraction built from known years and applied to earlier revenue) Tj ET
